WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
So the newest handoff here is for

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:05.020
beta. I want alpha. I asked the

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:08.013
project, watch. Ambiguous. It won't pick a

00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:09.847
job for me. Now I ask for

00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:11.550
alpha. That's the record I meant.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.630
now we're going to add task beta

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.470
to the same project and I have

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.470
two different jobs actually running and I

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.250
asked to resume a sample project without

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.310
naming either task. So what you can

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.870
see is I get ambiguous. It exits

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.150
eleven and no selected record. The tool

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.310
doesn't pick whichever one I happened to

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.863
save last. So I name alpha explicitly

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.903
and I get its record back. That's

00:00:31.903 --> 00:00:33.783
the question I needed the receiving session

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:35.343
to answer before I could actually carry

00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:36.370
on.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:36.887
So now I

00:00:36.887 --> 00:00:38.907
record a successor for alpha and mark

00:00:38.907 --> 00:00:41.127
that context stale. I use the first

00:00:41.127 --> 00:00:43.307
records ID as a predecessor. So the

00:00:43.307 --> 00:00:45.227
tool can tell me which revision I'm

00:00:45.227 --> 00:00:48.147
changing. I pick up alpha again, and

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.247
you can see it selects the new

00:00:49.247 --> 00:00:52.307
stale record. I get inspect only, exit

00:00:52.307 --> 00:00:54.580
10, and no continuation. I can still

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.340
inspect the earlier record with the show,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.540
but it says current false. I haven't

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.420
made the old context current just because

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.670
it looked more useful.
